r prankster friends Mayoi and Sakaki aren't much help. Especially Mayoi, as it gives her one more thing to tease Tsumiki over. Hime, the fifth member of their usual gang of five isn't much better, because she's not really well connected to reality anyway. Which leaves Tsumiki stuck in a quandary. Are she and Io just best friends? And is it worth risking that for what Tsumiki wants?\n\n(Source: Sentai Filmworks)"},"tags":[{"name":"Slapstick","rank":88,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Iyashikei","rank":83,"spoiler":false},{"name":"School","rank":82,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Nekomimi","rank":74,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Tsundere","rank":71,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Seinen","rank":70,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Kuudere","rank":64,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Heterosexual","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Female Protagonist","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Male Protagonist","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Female Harem","rank":40,"spoiler":false}],"titles":{"display":"Place to Place","english":"Place to Place","native":"あっちこっち","romaji":"Acchi Kocchi","synonyms":[{"language":"zh","source":"bangumi","value":"一起一起这里那里"}]},"trailer":null,"visibility":"general"}